{
  "example": "`fn[load]` moves to `src/config/load.rs` and its body is also edited. The\nmapped node's hash differs from the recorded one, so `habeas refactor` leaves\nevery record that read it unchanged and reports each one; those records stay\nstale until `habeas author` reassesses them.\n{cite}`requirements.refactor.outline_inputs`\n{cite}`requirements.refactor.whole_record`",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The example describes a concrete case: `fn[load]` moves to `src/config/load.rs` and its body is edited. The expected outcomes are that records which read it are left unchanged, each one is reported, and they stay stale.\n\n`tests/refactor.rs#fn[a_function_edited_while_moving_leaves_its_records_stale]` carries a `{test}` reference to the example. It covers every outcome:\n- **Scenario:** `project()` and `author(root)` write current evidence. `move_load(root, \" parse();\")` moves `load` to `src/config/load.rs` with a changed body. The test then runs `habeas refactor --map src/config.rs#fn[load]=src/config/load.rs#fn[load]`.\n- **Hash differs:** the test asserts the command succeeds and that the report contains the line `- evidence/rules.load.json: inputs[1]: src/config/load.rs#fn[load] no longer has the recorded hash`. This checks that the mapped node's hash differs and that the failing check is reported. `outline_inputs` requires the hash to equal the recorded one for the rewrite, and `whole_record` requires reporting with the failed check.\n- **Record left unchanged:** the test reads the bytes of `evidence/rules.load.json` before the run and asserts they are identical afterwards. This is the `whole_record` obligation that the whole record is left unchanged.\n- **Only one record read `load`:** `author` gives `rules.load` an input on `fn[load]`. `rules.check` reads only `fn[check]` and `fn[verify]`, so the single report line covers every record that read it.\n- **Stays stale:** `assert!(!errors(root).is_empty())` calls `validate_repository` after the run and shows the evidence is still invalid until it is reassessed. The test does not call `habeas author`, and the example does not need that.\n\nI found no gap: the assertions follow the example and the cited `outline_inputs` and `whole_record` requirements, and the test would fail if the record were rewritten or the failure went unreported.",
